v 3
d indsat: Indicator saturation for outliers and structural breaks (IIS SIS TIS MIS)
d
d  indsat is a library of indicator-saturation tools under one command. It detects outliers,
d  location shifts, trend breaks and coefficient breaks by general-to-specific selection over
d  saturating sets of impulse, step, broken-trend (linear/quadratic/cubic), differenced and
d  pairwise impulse, multiplicative, designed (volcanic, transitory change, ramp, user shape)
d  and user-specified indicators, with super and ultra saturation and common break dates.
d  The default search reproduces R gets::isat; split-half (Johansen-Nielsen; Nielsen-Qian) and
d  m-step Huber-skip estimators are included. Subcommands: indsat ardl (ARDL/EC with saturation
d  and PSS bounds test), loop, gauge, sim, and postestimation dates, path, plot, test, outlier,
d  distort, biascorr, bias, forecast, diag. Typed after regress, newey or ardl, indsat saturates the model in memory.
d  Journal-style tables and graphs.
d
d  KW: indicator saturation
d  KW: outliers
d  KW: structural breaks
d  KW: general-to-specific
d  KW: step indicator saturation
d  KW: ARDL
d
d Requires: Stata version 14.0; ardl (SSC) for indsat ardl
d Distribution-Date: 20261112
d Author: Merwan Roudane
d Support: email merwanroudane920@gmail.com
d
